+# Illustrative accepted draft: the blocked work raised as a story in the repo
+# it belongs to, in the category whose route can take the path.
+
+title: This repo's coder binding names its tools in the adapter's own names, so the coder seat engages again
+category: agents-repair
+
+Premise: this repo's .satelle/workflows/agents.local.toml restates the [coder]
+tools in another adapter's names, and node.alloc refuses the coder's
+engagement. The story is created and driven in this repo, by a session opened
+here; the agents-repair route dispatches no planner or coder and may change
+.satelle/workflows/agents*.toml and nothing else.
+
+Acceptance criteria:
+1. The [coder] tools in .satelle/workflows/agents.local.toml use the bound
+   adapter's own tool names, proven by `satelle validate` passing in this repo.
+2. A story engaged on the default workflow allocates its coder seat without a
+   node.alloc refusal, proven by `satelle story route` naming the coder.
